<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan cbank says liquidity will not be too loose.</title>
<headline>Taiwan cbank says liquidity will not be too loose.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's central bank on Thursday said local banks should not have false expectations that liquidity in the banking system would become too loose, hinting there is no room for interest rates to slide further.</p>
<p>&quot;Recent interest rate cuts and the expectations that future liquidity situation may become too loose are inconsistent with the central bank's 'stable to loose, but not too loose' monetary policy,&quot; Lee Sheng-yen, the central bank's banking department director told reporters.</p>
</text>
